# playpick cell: mode=walk boss=skyward (coverage label only -- evening steers
# at no boss, the walk starts at the door same as any other) spec=priest:discipline
# style=good size=25 difficulty=heroic view=820x1180,touch save=carried (behaves
# as fresh per #273 -- the dev-server port is pid-derived so localStorage never
# actually carries across separate playbot invocations). #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
# unlocks the 25-heroic tier the same way every other 25-heroic carried-cell
# script in this ledger does.
#
# Checked sessions.jsonl first: priest:discipline has three prior mode=walk
# appearances (wander/25-heroic/1280x800/fresh, melee/25-heroic/844x390/carried,
# flee/10-normal/844x390/carried, the last one this line's #6/#281 disprove-
# attempt) but never good-style, and never at this touch viewport (820x1180).
# It also has never had a `ui` check run on its own bar at 820x1180 -- the two
# prior priest:discipline `ui` calls were both 390x844 and 1280x800 -- so this
# is the first look at whether a healer's smaller ability set (heals, not a
# 5-slot dps bar) avoids the auto/ability overlap sliver 2026-09-29's
# druid:guardian session found at this exact viewport, or reproduces it under
# a different button layout. [[#6]]'s running theory is that 25-heroic crosses
# THE VIGIL clean regardless of style (five clean crossings on record, zero
# stalls) -- this adds a sixth style/spec combination to that count if it holds,
# and narrows it if it does not.
open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
tap back
tap raid
shot raid-setup
tap next
tap class:priest:discipline
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start
targets
ui
evening good 240 10
shot end
state
says
bill
